  "notes": "Two independent failure chains reported under one LER: (1) IPBD fire from incorrect joint compound (cause code X/Other per block 13 row 1, though the narrative describes a specific mechanism), leading to manual scram; (2) separately, following the scram, the 2A RPS normal power breaker tripped on overvoltage due to a degraded potentiometer (cause code B, Design/Manufacture/Installation/Construction Deficiency per block 13 row 2). Modeled two Cause nodes since block_13 lists two distinct cause codes for two distinct component failures; FORM-366 top-level cause_code/category (X/Other) governs the primary 'cause' node per rules, with the second cause captured as 'cause_b' for the potentiometer failure chain. RPS trip system independence and MSIV/containment isolation design context mentioned but not modeled as separate systems since not directly involved as backups per rule 6. Previous occurrence LER 374-2021-002-01 captured as stub per rule 9, key copied exactly as stated including leading unit digit."
